{"conjecture": "Test coverage is a submodular set function over the space of code paths, so each newly added test yields diminishing marginal coverage while interacting non-linearly with existing tests. As a system accumulates locally correct changes, the test suite's marginal value approaches a plateau (the submodular deficit), leaving structural coupling and emergent integration paths unobserved. Consequently, the cost of safely modifying the system rises not due to missing tests, but because the residual untested region is structurally irreducible—each subsequent change provokes combinatorial interactions the fixed test set cannot economically capture."}
